adopted: SHIPPING from S109. The label moves from d02d83b3cc22 because the
  LOGIC I/O fixes are in the shipping path, not behind a switch: the MEMS
  bridge is clocked on pins 119/120 and read on 121 (PIN_137 was a dead
  stub), cdc_i = o_dspb[2] with no strap in front of it, and PIN_70/109/110/
  111 are unassigned because D32 is out of requirements (PW 2026-09-25, D11).
  FLASHED to MW-D24-2 2026-09-25 and read back off the part:
  design_id 32'h4de0dd4a, cfg_bits 16'h0010. logic_flash.sh's default
  rollback and docs/d24-bench-logic-flash-log.md both point here now.
  Bench result on this bitstream: the MEMS lane went from ffffffff STATIC to
  CARRYING, 31 distinct in 32 reads, -64.76 dBFS, with the ADAU7002's 20-bit
  payload exactly in the top 20 bits of the word.
  Area cost against d02d83b3cc22, same tree otherwise: 881 vs 882 LE, 663 vs
  662 registers, 67 vs 69 pins, Fmax 65.78 vs 66.58 MHz. The reproducibility
  note on d02d83b3cc22 applies unchanged -- two builds of a label differ only
  in the .svf's date comment, so identity rests on the design ID read off the
  part.
